{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1168205-hunters-and-human-targets","id":1168205,"title":"Hunters and Human Targets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-16T09:43:20-08:00","id":1168205,"title":"Hunters and Human Targets","content":"So as we continue to pick away at Light Up the World, here's a little thought experiment. Where do you all think hunters draw the line at humans? Do they only go after the worst of the worst criminals, or are they all like the Union, not afraid to go after even street level punks? Are hate groups targets of theirs? What are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T10:04:44-08:00","id":1168209,"title":"","content":"Varies by Hunter to Hunter. By groups, though...<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey: They seem likely to draw a hard line and refuse to hunt actual humans. There might be certain exceptions (like Jack), but those are explicitly exceptions.<br /> VASCU: They explicitly hunt human serial killers. Granted, their tactics are non-lethal (in contrast to many Hunter organizations), but they don't seem to draw any distinction between mortal and monster as long as they fit the MO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T12:12:20-08:00","id":1168230,"title":"","content":"Yep. Depends on the group and individual. Theoretically, the most targeted humans would be the minions of various monsters, cultists, and supernaturally powered humans. For completely mundane criminals, only a few organizations have them as part of their mission statement (namely The Hunt Club, the Union, and VASCU). One of those groups is the legitimate police force seeking to incarcerate them, one is a group of vigilantes trying to keep their streets safe, and one is a group of serial killers who are picky about their targets (criminals arguably check all three boxes for the group's favorite victims.). Some like the Night Watch would theoretically encourage the killing of non-mundane threats (though they arn't really organized enough to have this as an overall goal), while others might non-lethally target them (a NZ guy might decide to video tape the crime or otherwise send evidence in to the police so they can handle it). Since this is an RPG, I would expect that most player groups who come across a nasty enough person will probably do something about it, regardless of what the overall groups think. A Lucifuge agent, an Aegis Kai Doru member, or a Knight of St.Adrian, or member most groups really could perform vigilante justice on the side without the higher-ups caring one way or the other. Several groups could actively punish vigilantes, a VALKYRIE soldier could be put in hot water for icing a murderer off-the books.<br /> <br /> Hate groups probably won't be the target of most hunter groups the same way a monster would be, unless they are the kind of group that regularly performs lynchings or otherwise &quot;has it coming&quot;. The Hunt Club being the obvious exception, and a particularly enthusiastic Union cell might target any hate groups that show their head. Otherwise, they would probably be targeted less actively. Union members might get into fist fights with the group, The Loyalist of Thule would naturally try to crush such groups, and players will probably dislike such groups and are likely to work against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}